00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.200
The same thing?

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.950
You've got an eye for it.
What's your name?

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:20.310
Keiichi Morisato, Mechanical
Engineering Department, 3rd year.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.150
I see. Morisato, eh?

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.480
I like you.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:29.650
Say, how about I also make one of these
and we have a little race?

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.960
A race?

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.290
Don't want to?

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:36.230
Well, this is all kind of sudden...

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.200
All this has made me want to race you guys.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.100
Not enough of a reason?

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.160
That's the only reason you...

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.700
I think it's a good idea.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:51.310
I'm sure it would be more fun to have two people
riding them rather than just one person.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:57.950
I think if you're sure it will be fun,
that's reason enough to do things.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.260
Hey, you're all right! What's your name?

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.160
My name is Belldandy.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.830
Okay, so Morisato and "Bell"...

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.800
You two are the best!

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.400
Okay, then, we'll have the race
right here in a week.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.170
Uh, what about us?
Okay, then, we'll have the race
