I don't believe this!

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:47.720
I don't believe this!

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:49.760
Who the hell tuned this suspension?!

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.990
Those guys still don't know jack.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.570
Belldandy?

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.500
Yes?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:05.900
I kinda see what it is you were
trying to say now.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.070
Great!

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:21.120
I kinda think we'd be in different classes...

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.290
Don't worry about that!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.950
Hey, you're the one who
wanted some practice!

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:31.170
Don't let its looks scare you.
After all, it's just a kid's toy.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.830
I'm no kid and that's no toy!

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.060
Sure, whatever...

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:36.840
Just you watch!

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:41.570
Banpei Hybrid Hydrogen-Powered
Extra-Special: Activate!

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.520
Good. The bike feels right...

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:11.430
This tuning is going to have a negative
effect on engine longevity.

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:13.970
Winning is gong to take more
than just horsepower...

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:17.510
What the heck are you doing?!

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.040
That's why I'm saying it's just a toy!

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.980
You CAN'T lose to something
like that, Banpei!

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:45.770
Guess I forgot to erase his attack program.

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.170
Listen, you...

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.070
Keiichi!

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:51.380
Hey...

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:55.050
Are you all right?! I heard a terrible crash!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.150
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:59.390
The bike's okay, too. See?

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:01.010
Oh, I'm so relieved!

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:06.390
I'm sorry, Keiichi, but I have a favor to ask.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.190
W-What's up?

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:16.840
Engine swap?!

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.010
What? Are you kidding me?!

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:21.580
We'll never have it set up in time
if we start now!

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.140
Our sponsor has put in a
very strong request.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:28.120
But the bike was just perfect during
today's practice! Why change it now?

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.620
If we go messing with it now, we'll never
get the machine working properly!

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.710
Let's just deny that request!

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:37.090
While it's true that the guy who gave
the order is just an amateur,

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:41.600
who thinks we'll win the race by
upping the engine performance...

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:46.000
this is still our valued sponsor,
who's keeping us in the race.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.570
You understand, don't you?

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:51.640
This project is going to be an all-nighter,
so I'll thank you in advance for the efforts.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:52.660
That's all.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.240
Jeez!

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:59.580
Damn, do you believe this crap?
It's probably cuz we haven't won
a single race this season...

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:00.050
It's probably cuz we haven't won
a single race this season...

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:05.340
Well, I can't blame them for being upset...

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:10.080
It takes sponsors to have a team...
and money to win...

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:14.930
I've had all I can take!

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:16.330
Chihiro?

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.660
Good evening!

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:43.190
Guess I kinda lost my cool, huh?

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:44.790
Not at all.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.460
This place is great!

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:50.620
You know it!

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:57.800
I was so glad when I knew I'd be able
to work in a place like this.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.880
I barely got any sleep...
I was working frantically.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:11.680
And now I have the fulfillment of being the
head mechanic that everyone can depend on.

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.710
But something just seems off!

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:21.690
You'd think I've been able to become
all that I wanted to be back then.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.130
Maybe I'm spoiled?

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.860
Maybe this doesn't make much
sense to you, huh?

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:33.130
No, it does.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:37.380
The wind blowing in your heart has shifted,

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.320
and it's no longer in harmony with
the wind blowing those around you.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.320
That's why a wind blowing from the past
became so nostalgic to you

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.790
and led you back to the Auto Club, right?

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:51.820
Lately, all I've been thinking about is the past.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:58.500
Then when I returned to the clubhouse after all
that time, there were people like Morisato there.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:08.740
That's why I decided that if I can race
Morisato and win as I am now,

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:11.940
I'll be able to get over this.
Why not, right?

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:15.210
Does that seem like an odd way
of thinking to you?

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:18.310
No, I understand it very well.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.290
You get it all, don't you?

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.590
Yes, I do. Because I'm a goddess.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:27.520
You really are a funny one, you know that?

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.960
Keiichi won't be so easy to beat, you know.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:36.170
Well, the fact I make my living through
racing means something, too.

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:38.970
And, I may have a few tricks up my sleeve.

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.100
You tell Morisato that.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:46.880
Well... I doubt Keiichi will care much, actually.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.170
Well, I'll see you later.

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:53.780
Hey.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:58.020
Are you in love with him? Morisato?

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:01.150
Yes!

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:13.840
Tamiya, Otaki, I know you guys
are here. Come on out.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.080
Y-You got us, Senior!

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:22.080
We missed you back on campus,
so we came all the way out here!

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:24.550
Oh, so that's why you're in there?

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.190
Whatever...

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:31.090
You guys have rounded up a good gang.

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:33.690
Which is why I think I won't have to
hold back when I take them on.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.660
I appreciate it.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.900
Oh, Chihiro...

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:40.600
You're too kind!

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:41.900
One more thing...

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.000
There's the whole matter of someone
"modifying" my baby...

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:46.970
It was just...

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:49.440
The club was running low on funds,
so we had no choice!

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:50.740
No excuses.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:55.010
We'll talk about this in detail some
other time. Be prepared.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.550
Oh, Chihiro!

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:00.080
You're too cruel!

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.290
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.390
Done already?

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:07.380
Yes.

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:09.430
Was Chihiro...

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:10.520
Yes?

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:15.070
Never mind... I guess it's all right.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.130
Let's go home.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:19.930
Sure!

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:26.310
All right then...

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:30.110
The winner will be decided after two laps
around the campus course.

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:33.250
Please be careful to avoid
endangering pedestrians.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.850
Who'll win?

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:38.920
Fool! Our Senior, Chihiro, obviously!

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:46.470
Okay, here we go.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.360
Ready...

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:50.170
GO!

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.000
Good luck to the both of you.

00:16:56.980 --> 00:17:00.340
I am rooting for Keiichi, though.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:02.650
Whoa!

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:03.650
What the heck?!

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:05.450
Is the Auto Club at it again?!

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:09.650
She's fast! How the heck did
she tune that thing?!

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:14.120
Hang in there! You've still got
a long way to go!

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.820
All right, now I feel a hundred
times more up to this!

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.100
I'll have to give this all I've got.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.100
Huh?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.630
This way!

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:27.200
Wasn't that just...

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:29.180
This way!

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:32.680
Uh... Better not worry about details right now!

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:34.580
Don't rush it, Keiichi.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:37.910
There's no way her engine will
hold up at that speed.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.990
I'll keep this pace.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.980
I'm sure my chance will come!

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:47.690
Oh! Here they come!

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.790
Chihiro!

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:55.130
Not good. I guess it's about time...

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:59.730
Morisato's a long way back, isn't he?

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:01.480
Damn right he is!

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.480
He's racing THE Chihiro Fujimi!

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:05.450
Ah! There he is!

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.410
The distance between him and Chihiro is...

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.880
Chihiro's stopped!

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:16.160
NO!
Her engine couldn't hold up
at that speed after all!

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.120
It can't be!
Her engine couldn't hold up
at that speed after all!

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:22.120
But she should have known that much...

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:25.000
No way!

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:27.090
She has a spare engine!

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.340
No one ever said swapping in
a new engine was prohibited.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.970
But still...

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:36.000
She shouldn't be able to get the most
speed out of a newly swapped in engine!

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:41.870
Those eyes... They don't look at anything
but what lies straight ahead.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:43.080
Just like mine back then...

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.120
C'mon! Give it a good push!
Just like mine back then...

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:45.350
Heave...
Just like mine back then...

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:46.690
Heave...

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:47.790
Chihiro!

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:48.760
Huh?

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:52.790
Come on, let's go to that mixer...
Uh, what are you DOING?

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:57.130
Ah, sorry, I'll have to pass.
I'm busy fixing this thing.

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:00.360
What's the point?

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.370
Well, it seemed like it'd be fun!

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:07.340
Back then...

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:11.970
I can do it!

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:21.490
Here they come!

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.530
Morisato's in front!

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:26.460
WHAT?!

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:27.550
No way!

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:31.500
Keiichi... Chihiro...

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:37.930
Chihiro?

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:40.070
Make it!

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.120
You lost.

00:19:57.120 --> 00:20:00.750
Yeah. But it's for the best, don't you think?

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:05.060
After all, I'm not the one Chihiro
was trying to beat.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.270
So you realized?

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.700
Yeah, somehow...

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:14.610
Still, the message you sent by racing
with all your heart got through.

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:15.700
Look.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:17.500
Morisato.

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:21.000
Thank you. It was a good race.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:23.510
You beat me good.

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:26.620
It looked like you were really enjoying it.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.790
I'd say you were, too, Senior!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.520
Huh? Me?

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:35.630
I thought the same thing when I watched
you repairing that old car.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:39.100
I thought, "this is the kind of person
I'd like to race."

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:40.630
Race me?

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:44.630
But you were even more amazing
when you were racing.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:50.230
The look on your face was so serious
and earnest... it was awesome.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:56.310
Did I say something funny?

00:20:57.350 --> 00:21:01.560
Well, that makes two of us!

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:02.520
Huh?

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:04.850
Thank you!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.790
I owe you some thanks, too.

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.830
I was able to put a lot of things
behind me thanks to you.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:14.600
But, I didn't do anything.

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:20.700
It was all thanks to Keiichi and your
own personal strength as well.

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:25.310
The two of you really are quite a pair!

00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:26.370
Yes!

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:32.650
I see...

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:37.950
I haven't changed a bit since then.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:43.160
Huh?!

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:47.400
Chihiro says she's going
to quit the works team.

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:48.600
Huh?!

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:51.740
She says it's because she wants
to design her own bike

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:54.970
to be used for fun rather than
just winning races.

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:58.680
That's awesome!
I'd love to try doing that, too!

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:02.450
She wrote that she knew you'd say that.

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:03.850
Uh... She did?

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:13.330
Yamashita Industries, Inc.
Interview Site

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:14.700
Yamashita Industries, Inc.
Interview Site
All right then...

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:17.730
Yamashita Industries, Inc.
Interview Site
Please explain what makes you want to
pursue employment with our company.

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:18.160
Please explain what makes you want to
pursue employment with our company.

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:19.350
Yes, sir!

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:24.360
There is something I want to do here!

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:33.770
Woh, it starts to shine

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:50.560
The gentle wind I felt on my cheek

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:59.330
Was the start of the miracles you brought

00:23:00.010 --> 00:23:07.470
As though my everyday life until
then had never existed

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:13.090
My new happy life, completely repainted

00:23:13.090 --> 00:23:16.490
In the colors of spring

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:21.430
Even waking up early, even traffic jams

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:25.830
Even heavy things to carry,
even sleepless nights

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:30.170
Somehow I feel thankful for everything

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:34.880
Let's create more and more of our miracles

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:42.710
Woh, whatever kind of morning

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:51.220
Woh, it starts to shine

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:54.620
Every day is a miracle

00:23:55.530 --> 00:23:58.230
I had thought our relationship was over...

00:23:58.230 --> 00:24:01.770
But as the plum trees blossom,
she remembers a past love.

00:24:01.770 --> 00:24:04.570
Next time, "Ah! A Goddess's Tears
and His Dream!"

00:24:04.570 --> 00:24:04.870
Ah! A Goddess's Tears
and His Dream!
Next time, "Ah! A Goddess's Tears
and His Dream!"

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:07.710
Ah! A Goddess's Tears
and His Dream!
I'm telling you that I'm not dating Urd!

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:09.440
Ah! A Goddess's Tears
and His Dream!
Be sure to watch it!
